<title>CANADA: Rogers CFO Savage resigns, Horn acting.</title>
<headline>Rogers CFO Savage resigns, Horn acting.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Rogers Communications Inc said its chief financial officer Graham Savage resigned to &quot;pursue other interests.&quot;</p>
<p>Alan Horn, the vice-president of administration, will serve as acting chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Savage will give up his title on August 31 and will resign December 31, the telecommunications company said.  </p>
<p>The shares dipped $1/8 to $7-1/4 in very light trading in New York before trading was halted.</p>
<p>Management change is sorely needed at the heavily leveraged firm, another analyst said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
